    77	   the canary; clear-and-never-restore left it empty.
    78	
    79	So the carrier is CLEARED (never redirected) at MODULE IMPORT time and is
    80	DELIBERATELY absent from the restore snapshot. Clearing rather than redirecting
    81	also keeps the DEFAULT arm of ``runtime_state_dir()`` (``HOME`` + slug, which
    82	Axis 1 already isolates) reachable for the whole suite; pinning the top of the
    83	precedence chain to a session path would make that arm unreachable and would
    84	force a matching edit into ``audit_carrier_overrides`` and
    85	``TestEnvContext.subprocess_env``. Production code keeps the override in full:
    86	nothing here touches ``_lib/runtime_paths``, and a test that exercises the
    87	override sets it for its own duration with ``mock.patch.dict``.
    88	## Axis 3 — the COLLECTION window (S326, 2026-08-24)
    89	
    90	pytest runs NO fixture under ``--collect-only`` — and in a normal run every
    91	test module is IMPORTED before the session fixture body executes. Import-time
    92	code that reaches an audit emitter therefore ran with the carriers still
    93	pointing at the live tree, and Axis 2 had already popped the whole-dir
    94	override, so nothing could redirect it. Measured: ``test_policy_mutations``
    95	replayed the policy corpus at import → 124 HMAC-signed, unattributable events
    96	per ``pytest --collect-only``; ``verify-counts.sh`` runs one before every
    97	commit → 19 runs / 2,356 links in 12 h = 79% of the live segment.
    98	
    99	Cure (``_redirect_collection_window``, import-time like Axis 2): snapshot the
   100	live log path FIRST (the WS-D1 comparator must still know what "live" means),
   101	then point the primary anchor ``CEO_AUDIT_LOG_DIR`` + ``CEO_PROJECT_STATE_DIR``
   102	at a throwaway ``ceo-collect-isolation-*`` tree. The session fixture keeps
   103	re-pointing everything at its own tree; at session END its restore now hands
   104	back the COLLECTION tree instead of the live value, which also closes the
   105	teardown-window escape (a late emit after the restore used to reach the live
   106	log). ``HOME`` is deliberately NOT touched here — it steers user-site package
   107	resolution for subprocesses, and the session fixture owns that dance. Guard:
   108	``.claude/hooks/tests/test_collect_only_audit_isolation.py``.
   109	"""
   110	
   111	from __future__ import annotations
   112	
   113	import atexit
   114	import os
   115	import shutil
   116	import tempfile
   117	from pathlib import Path
   118	from typing import Dict, List, Optional
   119	
   120	import pytest
   121	
   122	# --- Carrier-set enumeration (Codex R1 P0-3) -----------------------------------
   123	# Every env var that can steer WHERE an emit / HMAC sidecar / spool / lock /
   124	# fallback resolves. Path-valued carriers are pointed under the session tmpdir;
   125	# the rotate-bytes carrier is CLEARED so a stale-inherited value cannot influence
   126	# rotation. The enumeration lives HERE, exactly once. WS-C imports it.
   127	
   128	# Directory-level anchors we SET to the isolated tree. ``CEO_AUDIT_LOG_DIR`` is
   129	# the PRIMARY resolver for every audit path — ``audit_emit._audit_dir`` /
   130	# ``audit_hmac._audit_dir_from_env`` / ``spool_writer._state_dir`` all honor it
   131	# FIRST. ``HOME`` is the *fallback* the resolvers reach when ``CEO_AUDIT_LOG_DIR``
   132	# is absent. We redirect BOTH (plus ``CEO_PROJECT_STATE_DIR``) and CLEAR the
   133	# per-file overrides, so the entire audit/HMAC/spool surface resolves to the
   134	# isolated tree EVEN IF a test pops ``CEO_AUDIT_LOG_DIR`` mid-run (the fallback
   135	# then hits the redirected HOME's ``.claude/`` — still non-live). This is the
   136	# airtight structural guarantee (Codex pair-rail P0): a kernel resolver guard
   137	# would be the alternative, but ``audit_emit``/``audit_hmac`` are kernel-HARD-DENY.
   138	#
   139	# Redirecting HOME does break subprocesses that resolve TOOLING via the real
   140	# home (PyYAML in the macOS user-site). ``_activate_redirect`` therefore PRESERVES
   141	# ``PYTHONUSERBASE`` (real user-site) AFTER the HOME redirect. ``GNUPGHOME`` is
   142	# the OPPOSITE — it is CLEARED (not preserved), so gpg resolves under the
   143	# redirected HOME's empty ``.gnupg`` and the suite cannot reach the real signing
   144	# keyring (a real-keyring leak let sentinel ``.asc`` verification SUCCEED in
   145	# tests that require it to fail; see TOOLING_CLEAR_VARS). Net: isolate the audit
   146	# dir + the GPG keyring, without breaking user-site package resolution.
   147	#
   148	# ``CLAUDE_PROJECT_DIR`` is DELIBERATELY NOT redirected — it steers where hooks
   149	# find the PROJECT's ``.claude/`` files (policies, team.md, cookbook patterns),
   150	# is not an audit-location carrier, and redirecting it broke "the real repo is
   151	# configured" tests (test_flip_closures, test_cookbook_advisor_hook) for zero
   152	# isolation gain.
   153	AUDIT_DIR_CARRIERS = (
   154	    "HOME",
   155	    "CEO_AUDIT_LOG_DIR",
   156	    "CEO_PROJECT_STATE_DIR",
   157	)
   158	# Tooling env vars re-exported (to REAL values) after the HOME redirect so a
   159	# subprocess can still resolve user-site packages (PyYAML etc.).
   160	TOOLING_PRESERVE_VARS = ("PYTHONUSERBASE",)
   161	# Tooling env vars CLEARED after the HOME redirect so they resolve under the
   162	# redirected (isolated) HOME. GNUPGHOME → the redirected HOME's empty `.gnupg`,
   163	# so the suite cannot use the real signing keyring (tests that exercise GPG set
   164	# their own keyring_home/GNUPGHOME).
   165	TOOLING_CLEAR_VARS = ("GNUPGHOME",)
   166	# Carriers we explicitly CLEAR (the "or-clear" half of set-or-clear). These are
   167	# the per-file path OVERRIDES + tunables. We do NOT set them to fixed session
   168	# paths because ``TestEnvContext`` re-isolates per test by re-pointing only
   169	# ``CEO_AUDIT_LOG_DIR`` (+ LOG_PATH/ERR/LOCK) and RELIES on the KEY /
   170	# LAST_HMAC / CHAIN_LENGTH sidecars defaulting off ``CEO_AUDIT_LOG_DIR``. If the
   171	# session redirect pinned those overrides to a session path, every
   172	# ``TestEnvContext`` test's sidecars would stay stuck in the session dir while
   173	# its log moved to the per-test dir → chain-length/canary mismatch. Clearing
   174	# them (a) removes any stale parent-shell value that could point at the live
   175	# tree and (b) lets both the session anchor and each per-test anchor drive
   176	# resolution coherently.
   177	AUDIT_CLEAR_CARRIERS = (
   178	    "CEO_AUDIT_LOG_PATH",
   179	    "CEO_AUDIT_LOG_ERR",
   180	    "CEO_AUDIT_LOG_LOCK",
   181	    "CEO_AUDIT_KEY_PATH",
   182	    "CEO_AUDIT_LAST_HMAC_PATH",
   183	    "CEO_AUDIT_CHAIN_LENGTH_PATH",
   184	    "CEO_AUDIT_LOG_FALLBACK_PATH",
   185	    "CEO_AUDIT_LOG_ROTATE_BYTES",
   186	    "CEO_AUDIT_HMAC_DISABLE",
   187	)
   188	# Whole-directory overrides: carriers that select the ENTIRE runtime-state dir
   189	# at the TOP of the resolver precedence (``_lib/runtime_paths``, PLAN-182 W1).
   190	# They are NEUTRALISED at import time and NEVER restored inside the process —
   191	# see the module docstring, Axis 2, for the two measurements that force both
   192	# halves of that sentence.
   193	#
   194	# Deliberately NOT part of ``ALL_AUDIT_CARRIERS``: membership there means
   195	# "snapshot me and restore me at session end", and restoring this carrier
   196	# before interpreter shutdown is exactly the measured re-opening of the escape.
   197	WHOLE_DIR_OVERRIDE_CARRIERS = (
   198	    "CLAUDE_PROJECT_DIR_NATIVE",
   199	)
   200	# The full carrier surface — used by the WS-C partial-override rejection and by
   201	# the WS-E grep gate (every carrier must be enumerated in ONE place).
   202	ALL_AUDIT_CARRIERS = AUDIT_DIR_CARRIERS + AUDIT_CLEAR_CARRIERS
   203	
   204	# Sticky signals set into the (test) environment + inherited by children.
   205	TEST_HARNESS_VAR = "CEO_TEST_HARNESS"
   206	SYNC_MODE_VAR = "CEO_AUDIT_SYNC_MODE"
   207	# WS-D1 live-chain comparator: the resolved LIVE audit-log path captured BEFORE
   208	# the redirect. The drainer (which, post-redirect, cannot infer the live path
   209	# from env) reads this to decide whether a `_origin:"test"` spool is heading for
   210	# the live chain. Absent/unreadable ⇒ WS-D1 fails SAFE to no-quarantine.
   211	LIVE_LOG_SNAPSHOT_VAR = "CEO_AUDIT_LIVE_LOG_PATH_SNAPSHOT"
   212	
   213	
   214	def _neutralize_whole_dir_overrides() -> Dict[str, Optional[str]]:
   215	    """Pop every whole-directory override and return what was popped.
   216	
   217	    Import-time by design. All three conftests import this module while pytest
   218	    is loading conftests — BEFORE any test module is imported and long before
   219	    the session fixture body runs (verified: conftest import -> test-module
   220	    import -> session-fixture body -> test body). A fixture-time pop would sit
   221	    two steps later than the collection window.
   222	
   223	    The returned mapping is diagnostic only. Nothing restores it: the escape's
   224	    write happens at interpreter shutdown, so a restore anywhere inside the
   225	    process hands the carrier back before that write. The cost is process-local
   226	    and cosmetic — a runner that calls ``pytest.main()`` repeatedly sees the
   227	    carrier stay popped until it exits — and it is the deliberate trade.
   228	    """
   229	    popped: Dict[str, Optional[str]] = {}
   230	    for key in WHOLE_DIR_OVERRIDE_CARRIERS:
   231	        popped[key] = os.environ.pop(key, None)
   232	    return popped
   233	
   234	
   235	# Import-time side effect (the ONE in this module) — see the function docstring
   236	# for why it cannot wait for the session fixture. This module is pytest-only
   237	# (it imports pytest at the top) and is excluded from adopter installs by
   238	# scripts/install.sh, so no production hook can reach this line.
   239	NEUTRALIZED_WHOLE_DIR_OVERRIDES: Dict[str, Optional[str]] = (
   240	    _neutralize_whole_dir_overrides()
   241	)
   242	
   243	
   244	def audit_carrier_overrides(root: Path, *, sync_mode: bool = False) -> Dict[str, str]:
   245	    """Return the carrier env vars to SET so the FULL audit/HMAC surface resolves
   246	    under ``root`` (an isolated tmp tree), plus the sticky test signals.
   247	
   248	    Only the directory anchors + flags are SET; the per-file path overrides are
   249	    CLEARED by the caller (see ``AUDIT_CLEAR_CARRIERS``) so they default off
   250	    ``CEO_AUDIT_LOG_DIR``. Single source of truth for both the WS-A session
   251	    redirect (``sync_mode=False``) and the WS-C subprocess-env builder
   252	    (``sync_mode=True`` per S168 — a spawned child must write synchronously for
   253	    the parent to read deterministically).
   254	    """
   255	    root = Path(root)
   256	    home = root / "home"
   257	    audit = home / ".claude" / "projects" / "ceo-orchestration"
   258	    state = audit / "state"
   259	    overrides = {
   260	        "HOME": str(home),
   261	        "CEO_AUDIT_LOG_DIR": str(audit),
   262	        "CEO_PROJECT_STATE_DIR": str(state),
   263	        TEST_HARNESS_VAR: "1",
   264	    }
   265	    # NOTE: CEO_AUDIT_SYNC_MODE is DELIBERATELY NOT set here. It is orthogonal to
   266	    # *isolation* (it picks sync vs async-spool emit). TestEnvContext already
   267	    # defaults it ON per-test (SYNC_MODE_DEFAULT=True) and the rare async tests
   268	    # opt OUT via SYNC_MODE_DEFAULT=False — those tests rely on sync mode being
   269	    # ABSENT. If the session redirect forced sync mode globally, the async
   270	    # opt-out tests (e.g. the drain-cascade / async-flush probes) would run in
   271	    # sync mode, bypass the spool, and never reach the drain path they assert on.
   272	    # The WS-C subprocess builder sets sync mode itself (per S168) where a child
   273	    # must write synchronously for the parent to read deterministically.
   274	    if sync_mode:
   275	        overrides[SYNC_MODE_VAR] = "1"
   276	    return overrides
   277	
   278	
   279	def _resolve_live_log_path_snapshot() -> Optional[str]:
   280	    """Resolve the LIVE audit-log path under the CURRENT (pre-redirect) env, via
   281	    the production resolver. Returns a realpath string, or None on any failure
   282	    (the WS-D1 comparator fails safe to no-quarantine when absent)."""
   283	    try:
   284	        from _lib import audit_emit as _audit_emit
   285	        return str(Path(_audit_emit._log_path()).resolve())
   286	    except Exception:
   287	        return None
   288	
   289	
   290	# --- Axis 3 — collection-window redirect (S326) ----------------------------------
   291	COLLECT_WINDOW_PREFIX = "ceo-collect-isolation-"
   292	COLLECT_WINDOW_DIR: Optional[Path] = None
   293	IMPORT_TIME_LIVE_LOG_SNAPSHOT: Optional[str] = None
   294	
   295	
   296	def _snapshot_is_wellformed(value: str) -> bool:
   297	    """A usable inherited snapshot is an ABSOLUTE path that does NOT live
   298	    inside an isolation tree (a stale or redirected value is not truth).
   299	
   300	    Nothing about the name is pinned — not the basename and not the extension
   301	    (pair-rail r6 P2 + r7 P1): the documented ``CEO_AUDIT_LOG_PATH`` override
   302	    accepts any file (``/srv/audit/current.log``), and rejecting that inherited
   303	    truth made a worker re-resolve the DEFAULT path — so WS-D1 watched the
   304	    wrong file."""
   305	    return (
   306	        os.path.isabs(value)
   307	        and COLLECT_WINDOW_PREFIX not in value
   308	        and "ceo-suite-isolation-" not in value
   309	    )
   310	
   311	
   312	def _resolve_live_snapshot_outside_isolation() -> Optional[str]:
   313	    """Resolve the live log path with the whole-dir anchors temporarily removed
   314	    (pair-rail r2 P1). Used ONLY when an inherited snapshot was rejected: that
   315	    rejection is the proof the current anchor is an isolation redirect, so
   316	    resolving through it would hand the rejected path straight back. The
   317	    resolver then falls back to HOME; a result that still lives inside an
   318	    isolation tree is not truth either → ``None`` (the WS-D1 comparator fails
   319	    safe to no-quarantine when the snapshot is absent)."""
   320	    saved = {k: os.environ.pop(k, None) for k in ("CEO_AUDIT_LOG_DIR", "CEO_PROJECT_STATE_DIR")}
   321	    try:
   322	        candidate = _resolve_live_log_path_snapshot()
   323	    finally:
   324	        for key, value in saved.items():
   325	            if value is not None:
   326	                os.environ[key] = value
   327	    if candidate is not None and _snapshot_is_wellformed(candidate):
   328	        return candidate
   329	    return None
   330	
   331	
   332	def _redirect_collection_window() -> Dict[str, Optional[str]]:
   333	    """Point the primary audit anchor at a throwaway tree for the window between
   334	    conftest import and the session fixture body (module docstring, Axis 3).
   335	
   336	    Import-time by design, for the same reason as Axis 2. Three steps whose
   337	    ORDER is the whole point:
   338	
   339	    1. The throwaway tree and its ``atexit`` cleanup come FIRST (pair-rail r2
   340	       P2): ``atexit`` is LIFO and importing ``audit_emit`` (which step 2
   341	       does) registers the spool drain. Registering ``rmtree`` before that
   342	       import makes the drain run first and the ``rmtree`` last — the other
   343	       order let the drain re-create the tree we had just removed, leaking
   344	       one ``ceo-collect-isolation-*`` per process.
   345	    2. The live snapshot is captured BEFORE the anchor moves. An inherited,
   346	       well-formed value wins (pair-rail r1 P1: an xdist worker inherits the
   347	       truth AND a redirected anchor; re-resolving would return the parent's
   348	       collection tree). An inherited value that is NOT well-formed is a
   349	       redirected/stale one: resolve with the anchors removed (r2 P1) — never
   350	       through the anchor that produced it. Nothing inherited: resolve as the
   351	       process sees it (an operator-level ``CEO_AUDIT_LOG_DIR`` IS the live
   352	       location and must be honoured).
   353	    3. Only then the anchors move to the throwaway tree.
   354	
   355	    Returns the previous anchor values — diagnostic only, never restored (a
   356	    restore anywhere inside the process re-opens the escape at shutdown).
   357	    """
   358	    global COLLECT_WINDOW_DIR, IMPORT_TIME_LIVE_LOG_SNAPSHOT
   359	    # 1) tree + cleanup first (LIFO argument above)
   360	    root = Path(tempfile.mkdtemp(prefix=COLLECT_WINDOW_PREFIX))
   361	    atexit.register(shutil.rmtree, str(root), True)
   362	    audit = root / "audit"
   363	    state = audit / "state"
   364	    state.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)
   365	    # 2) snapshot before the anchor moves
   366	    inherited = os.environ.get(LIVE_LOG_SNAPSHOT_VAR) or None
   367	    if inherited is not None and _snapshot_is_wellformed(inherited):
   368	        snapshot: Optional[str] = inherited
   369	    elif inherited is not None:
   370	        snapshot = _resolve_live_snapshot_outside_isolation()
   371	    else:
   372	        snapshot = _resolve_live_log_path_snapshot()
   373	    IMPORT_TIME_LIVE_LOG_SNAPSHOT = snapshot
   374	    if snapshot is not None:
   375	        os.environ[LIVE_LOG_SNAPSHOT_VAR] = snapshot
   376	    else:
   377	        os.environ.pop(LIVE_LOG_SNAPSHOT_VAR, None)
   378	    # 3) move the anchors
   379	    previous = {
   380	        "CEO_AUDIT_LOG_DIR": os.environ.get("CEO_AUDIT_LOG_DIR"),
   381	        "CEO_PROJECT_STATE_DIR": os.environ.get("CEO_PROJECT_STATE_DIR"),
   382	    }
   383	    os.environ["CEO_AUDIT_LOG_DIR"] = str(audit)
   384	    os.environ["CEO_PROJECT_STATE_DIR"] = str(state)
   385	    # Per-file overrides inherited from the shell could still point a single
   386	    # sidecar at the live tree; clear them now, exactly as the fixture does.
   387	    for key in AUDIT_CLEAR_CARRIERS:
   388	        os.environ.pop(key, None)
   389	    COLLECT_WINDOW_DIR = root
   390	    return previous
   391	
   392	
   393	# Import-time side effect #2 (the pair with Axis 2 above) — see the docstring.
   394	COLLECTION_WINDOW_PREVIOUS: Dict[str, Optional[str]] = _redirect_collection_window()
   395	
   396	
   397	# --- Idempotent redirect state -------------------------------------------------
   398	# Holds the restore snapshot for the ONE fixture instance that performed the
   399	# real redirect. None ⇒ no active redirect (next session fixture will activate).
   400	_REDIRECT: Optional[Dict[str, object]] = None
   401	
   402	
   403	def _activate_redirect() -> Optional[Dict[str, object]]:
   404	    """Perform the real redirect once. Returns the restore-state dict for the
   405	    activating fixture, or None if a redirect is already active (no-op)."""
   406	    global _REDIRECT
   407	    if _REDIRECT is not None:
   408	        return None  # a sibling conftest's session fixture already redirected
   409	
   410	    # 1) The live log path was snapshotted at IMPORT, before Axis 3 moved the
   411	    #    anchor (resolving it here would return the collection tree). Fall back
   412	    #    to resolving only if the import-time capture failed.
   413	    live_log_snapshot = (
   414	        IMPORT_TIME_LIVE_LOG_SNAPSHOT
   415	        if IMPORT_TIME_LIVE_LOG_SNAPSHOT is not None
   416	        else _resolve_live_log_path_snapshot()
   417	    )
   418	
   419	    # 2) Capture the REAL PyYAML user-site BEFORE the HOME redirect so subprocess
   420	    #    Python tooling (e.g. lint-skills' strict-YAML leg) still resolves it.
   421	    #    Computed while HOME is still real.
   422	    #
   423	    #    GNUPGHOME is DELIBERATELY *not* preserved to the real keyring — it is
   424	    #    CLEARED below so gpg resolves to the redirected HOME's (empty) `.gnupg`.
   425	    #    Exposing the REAL keyring to the suite let sentinel `.asc` verification
   426	    #    SUCCEED inside tests that expect it to FAIL with no key (e.g.
   427	    #    test_mcp_canonical_guard's "PROTOCOL.md must block" — a signed PLAN-020
   428	    #    sentinel scopes PROTOCOL.md, so a real-keyring verify wrongly ALLOWED it).
   429	    #    Tests that genuinely exercise GPG set their own keyring_home/GNUPGHOME.
   430	    import site as _site
   431	    try:
   432	        _real_userbase = _site.getuserbase()
   433	    except Exception:
   434	        _real_userbase = None
   435	    tooling_overrides: Dict[str, str] = {}
   436	    if _real_userbase:
   437	        tooling_overrides["PYTHONUSERBASE"] = _real_userbase
   438	
   439	    # 3) Snapshot every carrier + the sticky signals + the snapshot var + the
   440	    #    tooling vars for exact restore at session end.
   441	    #    WHOLE_DIR_OVERRIDE_CARRIERS is ABSENT from this tuple on purpose: it
   442	    #    is the one carrier set that must NOT come back before the interpreter
   443	    #    exits (module docstring, Axis 2, measurement 2).
   444	    snapshot_keys = (
   445	        ALL_AUDIT_CARRIERS
   446	        + (TEST_HARNESS_VAR, SYNC_MODE_VAR, LIVE_LOG_SNAPSHOT_VAR)
   447	        + TOOLING_PRESERVE_VARS
   448	        + TOOLING_CLEAR_VARS
   449	    )
   450	    env_snapshot: Dict[str, Optional[str]] = {
   451	        k: os.environ.get(k) for k in snapshot_keys
   452	    }
   453	
   454	    # 4) Build the isolated tree + redirect the full carrier set.
   455	    tmp_root = Path(tempfile.mkdtemp(prefix="ceo-suite-isolation-"))
   456	    overrides = audit_carrier_overrides(tmp_root)
   457	    # Materialize the dirs so writers don't fail to mkdir mid-emit.
   458	    Path(overrides["HOME"]).mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)
   459	    Path(overrides["CEO_AUDIT_LOG_DIR"]).mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)
   460	    Path(overrides["CEO_PROJECT_STATE_DIR"]).mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)
   461	    os.environ.update(overrides)
   462	    # CLEAR carriers so a stale-inherited value can never point at the live tree.
   463	    for key in AUDIT_CLEAR_CARRIERS:
   464	        os.environ.pop(key, None)
   465	    # Re-assert the import-time neutralisation: a plugin, a conftest or an
   466	    # earlier test may have set a whole-dir override between this module's
   467	    # import and the first test. Not snapshotted above, so never restored.
   468	    for key in WHOLE_DIR_OVERRIDE_CARRIERS:
   469	        os.environ.pop(key, None)
   470	    # Re-export the real PyYAML user-site AFTER the HOME redirect (setdefault so a
   471	    # test that manages its own PYTHONUSERBASE keeps control).
   472	    for key, value in tooling_overrides.items():
   473	        os.environ.setdefault(key, value)
   474	    # CLEAR GNUPGHOME so gpg resolves under the redirected (empty) HOME/.gnupg —
   475	    # the suite must NOT reach the real signing keyring (see TOOLING_CLEAR_VARS).
   476	    for key in TOOLING_CLEAR_VARS:
   477	        os.environ.pop(key, None)
   478	    # Publish the live-log snapshot for the WS-D1 drain comparator (children
   479	    # inherit it). Only set when we actually resolved one.
   480	    if live_log_snapshot is not None:
   481	        os.environ[LIVE_LOG_SNAPSHOT_VAR] = live_log_snapshot
   482	
   483	    # 4) Reset spool_writer dir caches so the new env resolves immediately.
   484	    try:
   485	        from _lib import spool_writer as _spool_writer
   486	        _spool_writer._reset_caches_for_test()
   487	    except Exception:
   488	        pass  # fail-open; cache invalidation is hygiene, not correctness
   489	
   490	    _REDIRECT = {"tmp_root": tmp_root, "env_snapshot": env_snapshot}
   491	    return _REDIRECT
   492	
   493	
   494	def _deactivate_redirect(state: Dict[str, object]) -> None:
   495	    """Restore the env snapshot + remove the session tmpdir. Only the activating
   496	    fixture calls this (no-op fixtures pass ``None`` and skip)."""
   497	    global _REDIRECT
   498	    env_snapshot = state.get("env_snapshot") or {}
   499	    for key, value in env_snapshot.items():  # type: ignore[union-attr]
   500	        if value is None:
   501	            os.environ.pop(key, None)
   502	        else:
