     1	"""PLAN-119 WS-A — durable suite-wide audit-dir isolation REDIRECT.
     2	
     3	## Why this exists
     4	
     5	This repo **dogfoods an audit-emitting framework in its own repo against the
     6	real ``~/.claude``**. ``TestEnvContext`` (``_lib/testing.py``) isolates the
     7	audit dir *per test*, but that isolation is **opt-in**: any process that runs a
     8	hook / emits an audit event WITHOUT entering ``TestEnvContext`` writes to the
     9	LIVE ``~/.claude/projects/ceo-orchestration/audit-log.jsonl``. Those events
    10	carry HMACs computed under test conditions (or a different chain head), so
    11	``audit-verify-chain`` later reads ``tamper`` and ``audit-log.errors`` floods.
    12	S181 forensics: ~1690 of 1738 live-log lines were test/probe pollution.
    13	
    14	## What this does (Axis 1 — destination redirect)
    15	
    16	A **session-scoped autouse** fixture redirects the FULL audit/HMAC env carrier
    17	set (Codex R1 P0-3 — NOT just the four log vars) to a per-session tmpdir
    18	*before any test body runs*. A redirected process **physically cannot** append
    19	to the live log. This closes ~100 % of the pytest volume (the bulk of S181
    20	pollution) and carries **no suppression surface**: redirecting your own test's
    21	destination cannot silence someone else's real session (that was WS-B, dropped).
    22	
    23	A **function-scoped autouse** fixture additionally asserts (defense-in-depth)
    24	that the *production* audit-dir resolver (``audit_emit._audit_dir`` — imported,
    25	never re-implemented, per AC-A5) does not resolve to the snapshotted live dir,
    26	catching a test that mutates env back to the live dir mid-run.
    27	
    28	## Registration
    29	
    30	All three pytest conftests import the two fixtures by name so every collected
    31	test is covered regardless of which subtree pytest is invoked against:
    32	
    33	  - ``<repo>/conftest.py``                    (tree-wide — all ``testpaths``)
    34	  - ``.claude/hooks/tests/conftest.py``
    35	  - ``.claude/scripts/tests/conftest.py``     (net-new in PLAN-119 WS-A)
    36	
    37	The redirect is **idempotent** via a module-global guard: the first session
    38	fixture to run performs the real redirect and records the restore snapshot;
    39	later registrations (a sibling conftest's same-named fixture) detect the active
    40	redirect and become a no-op, so the three registrations never stack tmpdirs nor
    41	double-restore. Under ``pytest-xdist`` each worker is a separate process with
    42	its own module global → its own session tmpdir (plan R4).
    43	
    44	## Reuse by WS-C
    45	
    46	``audit_carrier_overrides()`` is the SINGLE source of the carrier-set
    47	enumeration; ``TestEnvContext.subprocess_env`` (WS-C) imports it so a spawned
    48	child inherits the exact same isolated destination — no second hand-maintained
    49	list to drift.
    50	
    51	## Escape hatch
    52	
    53	``@pytest.mark.allow_live_audit_dir`` (registered in ``pytest.ini``) marks the
    54	rare test that genuinely exercises the real resolver; the function-scope assert
    55	skips for it. Zero uses at ship; a ``validate-governance.sh`` grep gate keeps it
    56	at zero and CODEOWNERS requires security-engineer review to add one.
    57	
    58	## Axis 2 — whole-directory overrides (PLAN-182 W1 follow-up)
    59	
    60	PLAN-182 W1 gave the family a single resolver
    61	(``_lib/runtime_paths.runtime_state_dir()``) whose HIGHEST-precedence input is
    62	``CLAUDE_PROJECT_DIR_NATIVE`` — above the ``HOME`` Axis 1 redirects. An ambient
    63	value therefore steers runtime state OUT of the isolated tree no matter what
    64	Axis 1 does. Measured before this cure: a child ``pytest`` run whose only test
    65	body is ``assert True`` left ``audit-log.lock`` (0 bytes, 0600) and ``state/``
    66	(0700) in the operator's directory.
    67	
    68	Two properties of that escape decide the shape of the cure, and both were
    69	measured rather than assumed:
    70	
    71	1. **The write happens at interpreter shutdown**, not at import and not in the
    72	   test body. Probe: with the carrier set, ``from _lib import audit_emit``
    73	   listed the directory as empty BEFORE the import, empty AFTER the import, and
    74	   holding both entries after the process exited.
    75	2. **Any restore inside the process re-opens it.** A/B on a standalone child
    76	   run — clear-then-restore in a session-fixture finalizer left both entries in
    77	   the canary; clear-and-never-restore left it empty.
    78	
    79	So the carrier is CLEARED (never redirected) at MODULE IMPORT time and is
    80	DELIBERATELY absent from the restore snapshot. Clearing rather than redirecting
    81	also keeps the DEFAULT arm of ``runtime_state_dir()`` (``HOME`` + slug, which
    82	Axis 1 already isolates) reachable for the whole suite; pinning the top of the
    83	precedence chain to a session path would make that arm unreachable and would
    84	force a matching edit into ``audit_carrier_overrides`` and
    85	``TestEnvContext.subprocess_env``. Production code keeps the override in full:
    86	nothing here touches ``_lib/runtime_paths``, and a test that exercises the
    87	override sets it for its own duration with ``mock.patch.dict``.
    88	## Axis 3 — the COLLECTION window (S326, 2026-08-24)
    89	
    90	pytest runs NO fixture under ``--collect-only`` — and in a normal run every
    91	test module is IMPORTED before the session fixture body executes. Import-time
    92	code that reaches an audit emitter therefore ran with the carriers still
    93	pointing at the live tree, and Axis 2 had already popped the whole-dir
    94	override, so nothing could redirect it. Measured: ``test_policy_mutations``
    95	replayed the policy corpus at import → 124 HMAC-signed, unattributable events
    96	per ``pytest --collect-only``; ``verify-counts.sh`` runs one before every
    97	commit → 19 runs / 2,356 links in 12 h = 79% of the live segment.
    98	
    99	Cure (``_redirect_collection_window``, import-time like Axis 2): snapshot the
   100	live log path FIRST (the WS-D1 comparator must still know what "live" means),
   101	then point the primary anchor ``CEO_AUDIT_LOG_DIR`` + ``CEO_PROJECT_STATE_DIR``
   102	at a throwaway ``ceo-collect-isolation-*`` tree. The session fixture keeps
   103	re-pointing everything at its own tree; at session END its restore now hands
   104	back the COLLECTION tree instead of the live value, which also closes the
   105	teardown-window escape (a late emit after the restore used to reach the live
   106	log). ``HOME`` is deliberately NOT touched here — it steers user-site package
   107	resolution for subprocesses, and the session fixture owns that dance. Guard:
   108	``.claude/hooks/tests/test_collect_only_audit_isolation.py``.
   109	"""
   110	
   111	from __future__ import annotations
   112	
   113	import atexit
   114	import os
   115	import shutil
   116	import tempfile
   117	from pathlib import Path
   118	from typing import Dict, List, Optional
   119	
   120	import pytest
   121	
   122	# --- Carrier-set enumeration (Codex R1 P0-3) -----------------------------------
   123	# Every env var that can steer WHERE an emit / HMAC sidecar / spool / lock /
   124	# fallback resolves. Path-valued carriers are pointed under the session tmpdir;
   125	# the rotate-bytes carrier is CLEARED so a stale-inherited value cannot influence
   126	# rotation. The enumeration lives HERE, exactly once. WS-C imports it.
   127	
   128	# Directory-level anchors we SET to the isolated tree. ``CEO_AUDIT_LOG_DIR`` is
   129	# the PRIMARY resolver for every audit path — ``audit_emit._audit_dir`` /
   130	# ``audit_hmac._audit_dir_from_env`` / ``spool_writer._state_dir`` all honor it
   131	# FIRST. ``HOME`` is the *fallback* the resolvers reach when ``CEO_AUDIT_LOG_DIR``
   132	# is absent. We redirect BOTH (plus ``CEO_PROJECT_STATE_DIR``) and CLEAR the
   133	# per-file overrides, so the entire audit/HMAC/spool surface resolves to the
   134	# isolated tree EVEN IF a test pops ``CEO_AUDIT_LOG_DIR`` mid-run (the fallback
   135	# then hits the redirected HOME's ``.claude/`` — still non-live). This is the
   136	# airtight structural guarantee (Codex pair-rail P0): a kernel resolver guard
   137	# would be the alternative, but ``audit_emit``/``audit_hmac`` are kernel-HARD-DENY.
   138	#
   139	# Redirecting HOME does break subprocesses that resolve TOOLING via the real
   140	# home (PyYAML in the macOS user-site). ``_activate_redirect`` therefore PRESERVES
   141	# ``PYTHONUSERBASE`` (real user-site) AFTER the HOME redirect. ``GNUPGHOME`` is
   142	# the OPPOSITE — it is CLEARED (not preserved), so gpg resolves under the
