   371	      # -----------------------------------------------------------------
   372	      # Step: installer unsafe-write census (PLAN-185 W0, AC-3)
   373	      #
   374	      # The CLASS shellcheck above cannot see: a write whose DESTINATION was
   375	      # decided by an existence test. `-e` follows symlinks, so a dangling
   376	      # link at the destination sends the writer down the "nothing there yet"
   377	      # branch and the write lands OUTSIDE $TARGET (measured: 536 bytes,
   378	      # PLAN-185 §1). The census enumerates the forms PROVEN safe and treats
   379	      # everything else as `indeterminado` — fail-closed by construction,
   380	      # after three earlier passes that enumerated DANGEROUS forms and
   381	      # regenerated the same "form not modelled => fail-open" finding on
   382	      # every pair-rail round.
   383	      #
   384	      # validate.yml has NO `paths:` filter (it runs on every pull_request
   385	      # and every push to main), so this gate cannot fall into the S325
   386	      # "gate the change does not trigger" trap that the smoke-install path
   387	      # lists exist to avoid.
   388	      #
   389	      # Exit codes, both fail-closed — no `|| true`, no continue-on-error:
   390	      #   1 = a NEW blocking site, a DEAD baseline entry, or a malformed
   391	      #       baseline row (a row the loader cannot read waives nothing and
   392	      #       reports nothing, so swallowing it would let a corrupted
   393	      #       baseline look healthy);
   394	      #   2 = a census of ZERO sites, which FAILS by design — zero means the
   395	      #       search pattern broke, never that the repo got clean.
   396	      #
   397	      # RATCHET, not `--strict`, per the census §7 and OQ-1. MEASURED on the
   398	      # live tree 2026-08-26 with instrument sha256 25d6dcf3…: ratchet rc=0,
   399	      # `--strict` rc=1 on 424 indeterminate sites. A `--strict` gate would be
   400	      # born red and nothing could merge. That 424 MOVES with the instrument
   401	      # (the same tree answered 76 an instrument-generation earlier), so treat
   402	      # it as a dated reading, not a constant — measure, do not trust this
   403	      # comment. `--strict` is the target state once W1/W2 and the triage
   404	      # shrink the set; flipping it is a wave of its own, not a flag change.
   405	      #
   406	      # The instrument's own unit suite needs no step here: the
   407	      # `hook-tests-python-matrix` job runs the whole `.claude/scripts/tests/`
   408	      # directory (PLAN-186 W4a), so it is wired by membership — the same
   409	      # rule the double-collection note above states for the Wave C tests
   410	      # ("do NOT re-list them as paths").
   411	      #
   412	      # UNCONDITIONAL on purpose. The instrument ships in its own commit
   413	      # (PLAN-185 W0, 7383518) and is a tracked file, so there is no checkout
   414	      # of this workflow's own branch where it is legitimately absent. A
   415	      # defensive `if [ -f … ]` was considered and REJECTED: it converts a
   416	      # blocking gate into one that reports success when it ran nothing, which
   417	      # is the exact class the negative control in smoke-install.yml exists to
   418	      # prevent. If the instrument is ever missing, RED is the correct answer —
   419	      # it means the bundle did not land.
   420	      # -----------------------------------------------------------------
   421	      - name: Run check-installer-write-safety.py (PLAN-185 W0)
   422	        run: |
   423	          set -euo pipefail
   424	          python3 .claude/scripts/check-installer-write-safety.py
   425	
   426	      # ADVISORY, never a gate (PLAN-185 OQ-1). The ratchet above is blind to
   427	      # ONE thing by design: the baseline waives `indeterminado`, so that set
   428	      # can GROW without turning any check red. This step is that set's
   429	      # readout — one line per PR, so the debt is visible while OQ-1 is open.
   430	      # `continue-on-error: true` makes it structurally incapable of blocking
   431	      # a merge. Output is BOUNDED on purpose: `--strict` lists every site
   432	      # (424 lines today), which is a wall nobody reads, so only the summary
   433	      # line and a short tail are printed. The rc is captured immediately and
   434	      # printed rather than swallowed — `cmd > log; RC=$?` and never
   435	      # `cmd || true`, which would report success for every outcome.
   436	      - name: check-installer-write-safety.py --strict (advisory, OQ-1)
   437	        continue-on-error: true
   438	        run: |
   439	          set -uo pipefail
   440	          LOG="${RUNNER_TEMP:-/tmp}/iws-strict.log"
   441	          python3 .claude/scripts/check-installer-write-safety.py --strict > "$LOG" 2>&1
   442	          RC=$?
   443	          echo "--strict rc=$RC — ADVISORY; OQ-1 decides when (and whether) this becomes a gate."
   444	          grep -E '^--strict: ' "$LOG" || echo "(no --strict summary line — see the tail below)"
   445	          tail -n 15 "$LOG"
