     3	
     4	PLAN-011 Phase 11 (VP Engineering). Companion to ``session-graph-build.py``.
     5	
     6	The resume projection is a **read-only** view derived from the session
     7	graph (which is itself derived from audit-log + git). No new state is
     8	written. No audit events are emitted by this script. The output is a
     9	prompt fragment the CEO can feed to a fresh Claude Code session to
    10	reconstruct context for a plan that was interrupted.
    11	
    12	Usage::
    13	
    14	    session-resume.py --plan PLAN-010
    15	    session-resume.py --plan PLAN-010 --json
    16	
    17	Kill-switch::
    18	
    19	    CEO_SOTA_DISABLE=1 session-resume.py --plan PLAN-010
    20	    # -> exit 0, no output
    21	
    22	Behavior
    23	--------
    24	1. Locate the most recent graph under
    25	   ``$HOME/.claude/projects/<proj>/session-graphs/<plan>-<ts>.json*``.
    26	   - If the newest matching graph is **encrypted** (``.age`` or ``.gpg``)
    27	     AND the user has the matching key, decrypt in memory.
    28	   - If no decryptable graph exists OR the newest is older than 24h,
    29	     rebuild in-memory via ``session-graph-build.build_graph(...)``.
    30	2. Project the graph into a human-readable (or JSON) "resume" view.
    31	
    32	Stdlib only; Python 3.9+. Fail-safe on missing inputs — emits a
