    62	### Option C: `$HOME/.claude/projects/<project>/` (CHOSEN)
    63	
    64	- (+) Aligns with Claude Code's native memory location
    65	- (+) Per-user, per-project isolation
    66	- (+) Persistent across reboots
    67	- (+) Overridable via `CEO_AUDIT_LOG_DIR` env var for tests and
    68	  custom layouts
    69	- (+) One canonical location for every runtime artifact
    70	- (-) State is per-developer, not shared — a team setup would need
    71	  an explicit sync mechanism
    72	- (-) Onboarding doc must point at the out-of-repo location
    73	- (-) `CLAUDE_PROJECT_DIR_NATIVE` semantics are implicit; we may
    74	  need a formal env var in Sprint 3
    75	
    76	## Decision
    77	
    78	**All ephemeral runtime state lives under
    79	`${CLAUDE_PROJECT_DIR_NATIVE:-$HOME/.claude/projects/<project-slug>}/`.**
    80	
    81	Never under `.claude/` inside the repo tree. Env var overrides:
    82	
    83	- `CEO_AUDIT_LOG_DIR` — parent directory (defaults to the above)
    84	- `CEO_AUDIT_LOG_PATH` — log file path
    85	- `CEO_AUDIT_LOG_ERR` — errors file path
    86	- `CEO_AUDIT_LOG_LOCK` — lock file path (Sprint 2: `audit-log.lock`)
    87	- `CEO_AUDIT_LOG_ROTATE_BYTES` — rotation threshold (Sprint 2)
    88	
    89	Subdirectories (Sprint 2+):
    90	
   185	   the slug is the Claude Code path-based slug of the project's absolute
   186	   path (`/` replaced by `-`, e.g. `-Users-<user>-<path>-<repo>`) — the
   187	   SAME derivation Claude Code uses for `~/.claude/projects/<slug>/`
   188	   memory. The original "(~) derivation is implicit … Sprint 3 may align
   189	   them" note is hereby resolved in favor of the native slug: the bare
   190	   project name (the literal the code grew) COLLIDES for two checkouts
   191	   sharing a basename and is what produced the measured cross-tenant
   192	   mixing; the path-based slug cannot collide without the paths
   193	   colliding.
   194	2. **One resolver, imported by the whole family.** A single module owns
   195	   the derivation; no file in the family may re-derive the directory
   196	   locally (the ownership-verdict lesson: a locally-deciding branch
   197	   re-opens the class this closes). `CLAUDE_PROJECT_DIR_NATIVE` stays
   198	   the documented whole-directory override and MUST be consumed by that
   199	   resolver — an override with zero consumers is a spec fiction, which
   200	   is what this amendment repairs.
   201	3. **Family-atomicity invariant:** `audit-log.jsonl`, `audit-key`,
   202	   `audit-log.lock`, `audit-log.errors`, `.salt`, rotation siblings,
   203	   `backups/` and every sidecar resolve from the SAME base directory in
   204	   every configuration. Per-file env overrides (`CEO_AUDIT_LOG_PATH`,
   205	   `_ERR`, `_LOCK`) keep working for tests, but no supported
   206	   configuration may split the lock or errors from the log they guard
   207	   (the measured `CEO_AUDIT_LOG_PATH` split above is a DEFECT, cured in
   208	   W1, not a feature).
